<title>CHILE: COPPER - Codelco looks past strikes to new projects.</title>
<headline>COPPER - Codelco looks past strikes to new projects.</headline>
<byline>Paulina Modiano</byline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned copper firm Codelco has wrapped up wage contracts at all its mines, lifting for now the spectre of more strikes, and expects sharply increasing copper output starting in 1998, CEO Juan Villarzu said.</p>
<p>Trying to put an embarrassing pair of strikes at the Chuquicamata and Salvador mines this year behind it, Codelco is now counting on the Radomiro Tomic project and expansion at Andina to start changing its fortunes, Villarzu said, but added that a cultural problem among Codelco workers persists.</p>
</text>
